1
00:00:00,867 --> 00:00:01,800
<i>Why were you looking
at my stuff?</i>

2
00:00:01,933 --> 00:00:02,967
<i>You didn't have to go through
my bag!</i>

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,467
<i> I don't trust you.</i>

4
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,833
<i>If there's anyone you can't
trust here, it's you!</i>

5
00:00:06,967 --> 00:00:09,400
<i>I know that's why you want us
to stay,</i>

6
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:11,733
<i>because you want to put this
story on your vlog.</i>

7
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:13,433
<i>Joey already has the flash
drive,</i>

8
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:15,700
<i> but someone else is after it.</i>

9
00:00:15,833 --> 00:00:19,400
<i>I had to spend money cleaning up
the mess you made last night.</i>

10
00:00:19,533 --> 00:00:22,400
<i>It's good that Parak fixed
the mess you made.</i>

11
00:00:22,533 --> 00:00:24,600
<i>The investigators said
it was a gang war.</i>

12
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:27,033
<i> Even though we asked for help,</i>

13
00:00:27,167 --> 00:00:28,467
<i>the flash drive was still
damaged.</i>

14
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,500
<i>Is there really no way
to fix it?</i>

15
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:32,267
<i> You can't stay here!</i>

16
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,667
<i> You're still in danger.</i>

17
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,400
<i>I'm here to protect you,
to be your bodyguard.</i>

18
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:39,067
<i>I think the people we
encountered last night</i>

19
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:40,433
<i> had connections to the police.</i>

20
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:43,800
<i>Do you have any other info
that might help us?</i>

21
00:00:43,933 --> 00:00:47,233
<i>And there's a name that keeps
coming up, the codename, Parak.</i>

22
00:00:47,367 --> 00:00:49,700
<i> I'm just here at Joey's house.</i>

23
00:00:49,833 --> 00:00:51,500
<i>I think she's up
to something bad.</i>

24
00:00:51,633 --> 00:00:52,500
<i> Godfather.</i>

25
00:00:52,633 --> 00:00:54,000
<i>What evidence are you talking
about?</i>

26
00:01:13,933 --> 00:01:16,400
Are you sure about the contents
here, Joey?

27
00:01:16,533 --> 00:01:18,133
Yes.

28
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:20,600
And I'm also sure that
that woman and her companion

29
00:01:20,733 --> 00:01:22,167
are the ones Who really killed
Ramon.

30
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:25,200
Joey, besides you,
who else knows about this?

31
00:01:25,333 --> 00:01:27,033
Just Peter and me.

32
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:28,000
Are you sure?

33
00:01:28,133 --> 00:01:30,267
But the thing is, it's broken.

34
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:32,967
Maybe you know someone
who can fix it.

35
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:33,867
There is.

36
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,900
I know someone I can ask
to restore it.

37
00:01:37,033 --> 00:01:38,367
Sorry, Godfather,

38
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,100
I should have told you
that a long time ago.

39
00:01:42,267 --> 00:01:44,500
How I wish it didn't get lost,
it wasn't broken

40
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:48,533
so this wouldn't be happening
to Father now.

41
00:01:48,667 --> 00:01:51,000
Stop it, Joey.
Don't cry anymore.

42
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:52,933
Your Godfather is here.

43
00:01:53,067 --> 00:01:54,633
I won't neglect you.

44
00:01:54,767 --> 00:01:56,167
I'll help you.

45
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:59,833
I'll go to those who can restore
this flash drive.

46
00:01:59,967 --> 00:02:01,033
Joey,

47
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:06,200
promise me that no one else will
find out about this.

48
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:07,300
Is that possible?

49
00:02:07,433 --> 00:02:08,367
Yes, Godfather.

50
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:10,267
Okay.

51
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:14,500
You're really my last hope
to help Father.

52
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,500
So thank you, Godfather.

53
00:02:16,633 --> 00:02:17,633
Yes.

54
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:19,967
I feel sorry for her.

55
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,567
She's crying again.

56
00:02:23,333 --> 00:02:25,867
I want to go to Joey.

57
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,967
I can't see her crying like
that.

58
00:02:29,467 --> 00:02:30,967
How long have you liked her?

59
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:33,433
What?

60
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:35,467
No.

61
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,467
I don't like her.
I'm just concerned.

62
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:40,733
We're just friends.

63
00:02:40,867 --> 00:02:41,933
Just friends.

64
00:02:43,167 --> 00:02:45,200
- Okay.
- I'm telling the truth!

65
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:46,467
You know what?

66
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:49,267
Just mind your own business,
Oppa.

67
00:02:58,133 --> 00:02:59,233
That's enough.

68
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:02,400
Don't worry. I'll help you.

69
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:04,667
I'll help you, okay?

70
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:05,833
Thank you, Godfather.

71
00:03:05,967 --> 00:03:08,700
- You're really kind to us.
- Of course.

72
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:34,833
Boss Budol?

73
00:03:38,167 --> 00:03:39,667
Joey, where did you come from?

74
00:03:42,333 --> 00:03:44,133
Why is this Korean here?

75
00:03:45,867 --> 00:03:47,300
He lives here.

76
00:03:49,667 --> 00:03:50,867
Wait a minute.

77
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,167
Why do you ask
so many questions?

78
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:56,167
Shouldn't I be the one
asking you questions?

79
00:03:57,433 --> 00:04:01,033
What are you doing here?
How did you know I live here?

80
00:04:01,167 --> 00:04:02,600
You're a stalker too, right?

81
00:04:02,733 --> 00:04:04,000
Me, a stalker?

82
00:04:05,633 --> 00:04:06,933
Well, this guy...

83
00:04:07,067 --> 00:04:08,533
He now lives here.

84
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,033
Hey, you.

85
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:12,833
What are you doing here?

86
00:04:12,967 --> 00:04:15,167
I'm staying here now.

87
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:16,600
I'm Joey's bodyguard.

88
00:04:16,733 --> 00:04:17,800
Bodyguard?

89
00:04:17,933 --> 00:04:20,267
Self-appointed bodyguard.

90
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,500
He volunteered himself?

91
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:23,567
Yeah.

92
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:25,367
That's okay?

93
00:04:25,500 --> 00:04:29,233
Wherever Joey goes,
there's a bodyguard.

94
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:32,967
You immediately believed
that was all he wanted to do?

95
00:04:33,100 --> 00:04:36,133
So what if there was something
else he wanted to do?

96
00:04:36,267 --> 00:04:37,567
Like the flash drive.

97
00:04:37,700 --> 00:04:39,400
I'm sure not.

98
00:04:39,533 --> 00:04:41,567
He even took me to my
Godfather, the policeman,

99
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,833
to give me the flash drive.

100
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:43,767
What?

101
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,433
You gave the flash drive
to a policeman?

102
00:04:45,567 --> 00:04:48,400
Joey, that's the main reason
I came here.

103
00:04:48,533 --> 00:04:50,300
Your father wants to warn you

104
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:52,800
because we don't know who
the real allies are.

105
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:54,967
Hey, stay cool.

106
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:56,633
No need to shout.

107
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:03,133
Okay, listen to me.

108
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,600
Your father is worried

109
00:05:04,733 --> 00:05:08,900
because he thinks our enemies
have a police conspirator.

110
00:05:09,033 --> 00:05:11,067
So, Joey, you shouldn't trust
just anyone.

111
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:13,633
Please, my Godfather isn't like
that.

112
00:05:13,767 --> 00:05:16,567
He thinks of us as family,
so don't judge him.

113
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:18,967
Okay, fine, okay. Your uncle...

114
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:20,633
I mean your Godfather...

115
00:05:20,767 --> 00:05:22,233
Let's just say he's decent,

116
00:05:22,367 --> 00:05:24,367
but what about the people he'll
approach?

117
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,067
The ones who will see the video?

118
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,600
Aren't you thinking, Joey?

119
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:29,500
Can he trust that?

120
00:05:49,067 --> 00:05:50,700
Matias, why?

121
00:05:50,833 --> 00:05:52,233
What now?

122
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:53,900
<i> What happened to you?</i>

123
00:05:54,033 --> 00:05:55,467
Why did you suddenly
say goodbye?

124
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,533
The meeting isn't over yet.

125
00:05:56,667 --> 00:05:58,400
You know,
you're such a smart-aleck!

126
00:05:58,533 --> 00:05:59,567
What do you care?

127
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:01,833
I have something important
to do.

128
00:06:01,967 --> 00:06:04,100
More important than Berdugo's
orders?

129
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:07,700
Or maybe you have another boss?
You're not loyal to the group.s

130
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:10,967
What?

131
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,600
Why aren't you talking?

132
00:06:12,733 --> 00:06:13,800
Is it because you really don't
want to say

133
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:15,567
what important thing you did?

134
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,300
I'll just remind you, okay?

135
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:19,367
Maybe you've forgotten,

136
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:22,700
I'm still a policeman, Matias,
okay?

137
00:06:22,833 --> 00:06:26,033
I have to keep up
with my police work

138
00:06:26,167 --> 00:06:29,667
so I can protect Berdugo's
group.

139
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,867
Now, you know.

140
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:34,200
Okay, let's meet tonight
at the warehouse.

141
00:06:34,333 --> 00:06:36,300
Make sure you're on time.

142
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:42,000
What do you think
of my Godfather?

143
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:43,000
A fool?

144
00:06:44,233 --> 00:06:45,267
Of course, he's smart.

145
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:48,433
He knows who he should trust
and not.

146
00:06:48,567 --> 00:06:50,133
You're so close-minded.

147
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:55,200
Your father himself said don't
easily trust,

148
00:06:55,333 --> 00:06:58,100
but you're so stubborn, Joey.

149
00:06:58,233 --> 00:07:00,133
You still won't listen.

150
00:07:00,267 --> 00:07:01,433
That's right.

151
00:07:01,567 --> 00:07:04,200
So I shouldn't trust you either,
right?

152
00:07:08,633 --> 00:07:11,367
I'll talk to my father
about what I'm doing.

153
00:07:12,833 --> 00:07:14,733
Don't worry about us anymore.

154
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:16,367
We can do this.

155
00:07:17,567 --> 00:07:18,867
You can go now.

156
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,067
Boss Budol, you heard that,
right?

157
00:07:22,200 --> 00:07:24,167
You can go now.

158
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,833
Fine.

159
00:07:25,967 --> 00:07:29,867
But don't come running to me
asking for my help.

160
00:07:30,000 --> 00:07:31,300
I really won't.

161
00:07:35,533 --> 00:07:37,200
What? Should I walk you out?

162
00:07:37,333 --> 00:07:39,267
Maybe you'll get lost
in our house?

163
00:07:47,767 --> 00:07:48,733
Here,

164
00:07:50,733 --> 00:07:52,333
what do you think?
Can you do it?

165
00:07:52,467 --> 00:07:53,933
Where did this come from, Sir?

166
00:07:54,067 --> 00:07:55,367
Don't ask anymore.

167
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,233
The damage is so bad.

168
00:07:57,367 --> 00:07:59,567
It will take a while
for me to do this.

169
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,400
Here's my down payment.

170
00:08:09,533 --> 00:08:11,367
Once you fix that,
there'll be more to come.

171
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:13,067
What? Can you do it?

172
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:14,300
That's automatic, Sir.

173
00:08:14,433 --> 00:08:16,300
I'll take care of it.

174
00:08:16,433 --> 00:08:18,067
I'll get back to you, okay?

175
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,333
Hurry up.

176
00:08:19,467 --> 00:08:20,833
Okay, Sir, okay.

177
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:27,733
A lot of people are asking me
why we don't have an update...

178
00:08:30,033 --> 00:08:32,367
on the case of Major Miguel
Delgado.

179
00:08:33,567 --> 00:08:37,200
There might be more
than meets the eye.

180
00:08:37,333 --> 00:08:39,033
People...

181
00:08:41,933 --> 00:08:46,167
Details that need to be
confirmed and people

182
00:08:46,300 --> 00:08:49,767
that need to be identified with
the involvement of...

183
00:08:51,967 --> 00:08:53,633
Of course, it's hard to...

184
00:08:56,867 --> 00:08:58,200
Cut, cut, cut.

185
00:08:59,700 --> 00:09:00,667
Sorry, sorry.

186
00:09:03,467 --> 00:09:05,767
What's up, boss?
The take is okay.

187
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:08,167
Are you okay?

188
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:10,667
Are you not in the mood?

189
00:09:12,433 --> 00:09:13,533
Sorry, sorry.

190
00:09:13,667 --> 00:09:14,700
Sorry, guys.

191
00:09:15,967 --> 00:09:17,900
You're thinking about something.

192
00:09:18,033 --> 00:09:19,400
Come on, what's that?

193
00:09:22,167 --> 00:09:24,333
Okay, I'm pissed off
with that Joey.

194
00:09:24,467 --> 00:09:29,400
She's the one I'm helping
but she's the one who refuses.

195
00:09:31,467 --> 00:09:33,667
That's the thing.

196
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:34,967
This is the first time
I've seen you

197
00:09:35,100 --> 00:09:36,233
being bothered by a woman.

198
00:09:36,367 --> 00:09:38,133
She knows how to piss you off.

199
00:09:38,267 --> 00:09:40,467
You're not used to being
rejected, are you?

200
00:09:41,900 --> 00:09:44,167
Come on, Boss, let it go.

201
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:47,267
If she doesn't want your help,
then let her be, right?

202
00:09:48,467 --> 00:09:50,233
It's not like that.

203
00:09:50,367 --> 00:09:51,200
Because somehow,

204
00:09:51,333 --> 00:09:53,767
I feel responsible
for what happened

205
00:09:53,900 --> 00:09:55,267
to Major Miguel Delgado.

206
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:59,900
I gave him my word
that I would help him.

207
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:01,500
That's the dilemma.

208
00:10:03,633 --> 00:10:04,767
Anyway...

209
00:10:06,167 --> 00:10:08,200
We have to do this.
Let's get back to work.

210
00:10:11,167 --> 00:10:12,833
Okay. Game.

211
00:10:14,733 --> 00:10:15,800
Are you ready?

212
00:10:20,233 --> 00:10:21,467
Fellow Tiradas!

213
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,867
This is a surprise inspection!

214
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,100
Hey, move to the side!

215
00:10:40,433 --> 00:10:41,367
Get down there.

216
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:42,500
Hurry!

217
00:10:42,633 --> 00:10:43,533
You're there already.

218
00:11:13,433 --> 00:11:14,300
Yes, Mother.

219
00:11:14,433 --> 00:11:17,700
I'm not neglecting my studies.

220
00:11:17,833 --> 00:11:19,367
That's good, Joey.

221
00:11:19,500 --> 00:11:22,200
Go to bed early.
You still have school tomorrow.

222
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:25,533
Mother,

223
00:11:25,667 --> 00:11:29,633
can you go see Father?

224
00:11:29,767 --> 00:11:32,567
Just tell him I'm fine

225
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:36,233
because I gave the flash drive
to Godfather.

226
00:11:36,367 --> 00:11:38,900
Oh my God,
it's good you did that.

227
00:11:39,033 --> 00:11:41,500
When the video comes out,
when the truth comes out,

228
00:11:41,667 --> 00:11:44,267
everyone will know that Father
was just setup.

229
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:47,833
And maybe that Golda
was just an accomplice.

230
00:11:52,767 --> 00:11:53,733
Mother...

231
00:11:55,433 --> 00:12:01,300
When all this is over,
can you forgive Father?

232
00:12:01,433 --> 00:12:03,367
I'm trying, my child.

233
00:12:05,367 --> 00:12:06,733
Even now,

234
00:12:08,067 --> 00:12:13,700
I'm trying to remove and get rid
of the pain I feel in my heart.

235
00:12:15,867 --> 00:12:18,667
I also want our family
to be complete, Joey.

236
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,867
Of course, Mother,
that will happen,

237
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:27,500
especially now that Godfather
Diego is going to help us.

238
00:12:27,633 --> 00:12:30,033
Late as usual.

239
00:12:36,533 --> 00:12:38,433
Did your men find anything?

240
00:12:39,733 --> 00:12:42,867
They didn't find a flash drive
at the crime scene.

241
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,367
Even the bodies that were there,
they tried to search them.

242
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:48,500
They didn't find anything.

243
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:53,033
It means that girl
got the flash drive!

244
00:12:53,167 --> 00:12:55,167
Did she think I would stop
bothering her?

245
00:12:55,300 --> 00:12:57,433
We're not done yet.

246
00:12:58,667 --> 00:13:02,000
You know, if I were you,
I would stop that.

247
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,533
You want to know why?

248
00:13:05,667 --> 00:13:06,533
First,

249
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:10,000
look, you look weak.

250
00:13:10,133 --> 00:13:12,733
Because you're scared
of that video.

251
00:13:12,867 --> 00:13:16,433
Second, you haven't seen any
videos coming out yet, have you?

252
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:18,867
Have you seen any?

253
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:21,100
You, have you seen any?
None, haven't you?

254
00:13:21,267 --> 00:13:22,700
None yet.

255
00:13:22,833 --> 00:13:24,867
Don't mind Lisa's strategy.

256
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:29,500
Your job is to carry out
Berdugo's orders,

257
00:13:30,733 --> 00:13:32,467
to kill Delgado!

258
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:41,667
Continue the search.

259
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:44,000
- Yes, Sir.
- Let's go outside.

260
00:13:56,233 --> 00:13:57,233
What is this?

261
00:13:57,367 --> 00:13:58,900
Why are you hiding this?

262
00:14:00,733 --> 00:14:03,067
Cruz, I was set up,

263
00:14:03,200 --> 00:14:05,967
and that's the only way
I can find out who did this.

264
00:14:07,133 --> 00:14:09,800
Until now, you still believe
that?

265
00:14:13,533 --> 00:14:14,867
Hide it very well.

266
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,100
Maybe next time someone else
will get it.

267
00:14:18,433 --> 00:14:19,867
Do you believe me?

268
00:14:21,167 --> 00:14:23,200
I'm sorry, I can't do anything.

269
00:14:23,333 --> 00:14:26,933
There's evidence against you,
the gun in your car.

270
00:14:27,067 --> 00:14:30,400
It's not mine. I was set up.

271
00:14:30,567 --> 00:14:31,567
Who?

272
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:37,600
I think it's the police
from Manila.

273
00:14:39,033 --> 00:14:40,233
Possible,

274
00:14:40,367 --> 00:14:44,333
but it could also have been in
your car before they arrived.

275
00:14:44,467 --> 00:14:46,300
Maybe someone else put it there.

276
00:14:49,933 --> 00:14:50,700
What?

277
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:51,967
Can you do it?

278
00:14:53,667 --> 00:14:58,033
Otherwise, I will just do it
and kill Delgado.

279
00:14:58,167 --> 00:15:00,167
Why are you so eager to kill?

280
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,567
Don't meddle with my job.

281
00:15:02,733 --> 00:15:04,300
I'll take care of that.

282
00:15:04,433 --> 00:15:05,967
Why do you seem to be delaying
it?

283
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,667
Is it because you feel sorry
for him,

284
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:09,600
and Delgado is your fellow cop?

285
00:15:09,733 --> 00:15:11,400
But when you killed Ramon,

286
00:15:11,533 --> 00:15:13,133
you didn't care about him,
right?

287
00:15:13,267 --> 00:15:14,433
Here...

288
00:15:14,567 --> 00:15:16,067
Let me tell you, it seems like
your brain can't comprehend it.

289
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:18,700
I'm just taking care of this
partnership.

290
00:15:18,833 --> 00:15:22,333
You know, right, the situation
is hot right now!

291
00:15:22,467 --> 00:15:25,067
If I kill that Delgado now,

292
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:27,700
what, there'll be another
investigation?

293
00:15:27,833 --> 00:15:30,367
Especially since it's inside
the prison cell!

294
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:32,533
I won't let myself get caught!

295
00:15:32,667 --> 00:15:35,600
You'll lose police protection!

296
00:15:35,767 --> 00:15:39,233
If you're really good,
you won't get caught.

297
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:42,067
That's why we hired you,

298
00:15:42,200 --> 00:15:43,933
because you have strong
protection.

299
00:15:44,067 --> 00:15:45,300
Your Godfather is strong.

300
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:47,867
What's the point of being
a policeman's nephew

301
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,967
if you're just a coward?

302
00:15:53,833 --> 00:15:57,067
<i>There's evidence against you,
the gun in your car.</i>

303
00:15:57,200 --> 00:16:00,300
<i>It's not mine. I was set it up.</i>

304
00:16:00,433 --> 00:16:04,400
<i>But it could have been
in your car before they arrived.</i>

305
00:16:04,533 --> 00:16:06,167
<i>Maybe someone else put it there.</i>

306
00:16:14,667 --> 00:16:16,233
Who did that?

307
00:16:20,533 --> 00:16:23,267
<i>My car doesn't suit
your appearance.</i>

308
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:24,867
<i> Your watch, upgraded.</i>

309
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:25,933
<i> Your shoes too!</i>

310
00:16:26,067 --> 00:16:28,100
<i>Buddy, wait a minute. My wallet.</i>

311
00:16:28,233 --> 00:16:31,500
<i>Please check the bag.
Here. I got it.</i>

312
00:17:03,600 --> 00:17:04,833
It's Diego...

313
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:08,400
Impossible.

314
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:14,267
Who told you I was a coward?

315
00:17:17,500 --> 00:17:19,867
I'm not a coward.

316
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:23,267
I'm not just like you who don't
use your brain.

317
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:25,033
As for, I'm thinking.

318
00:17:25,167 --> 00:17:26,633
You guys are impulsive
and rush things.

319
00:17:26,767 --> 00:17:31,767
Just follow orders,
or Berdugo will take you down.

320
00:17:31,900 --> 00:17:34,233
I'll probably end up finishing
Delgado off!

321
00:17:41,967 --> 00:17:44,533
Joey's so stubborn.

322
00:17:44,667 --> 00:17:47,167
She just acts impulsively.

323
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,800
She doesn't even think.

324
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:51,700
Why? What did she do?

325
00:17:51,833 --> 00:17:55,533
Miguel, she gave the flash drive
to her Godfather Diego.

326
00:17:56,900 --> 00:18:02,300
I just hope Diego doesn't get
close to bad people.

327
00:18:04,367 --> 00:18:05,300
You know,

328
00:18:06,767 --> 00:18:08,833
Diego is the wrong guy.

329
00:18:11,367 --> 00:18:12,567
What do you mean?

330
00:18:14,333 --> 00:18:15,367
Diego...

331
00:18:16,467 --> 00:18:17,600
is Parak.

332
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:26,067
Isn't he your best friend?

333
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,767
Me too, I can't believe it,

334
00:18:31,633 --> 00:18:33,967
but the notebook is referring
to him.

335
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:35,133
But how?

336
00:18:35,267 --> 00:18:37,567
That "Bulalakaw",

337
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:38,867
shooting star...

338
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,767
That's the firing range where
Diego and I go.

339
00:18:41,900 --> 00:18:45,000
Then, the stall number is there.

340
00:18:45,133 --> 00:18:47,467
I think that's where he meets
Ramon.

341
00:18:47,600 --> 00:18:50,000
And the gun that was found
in my car,

342
00:18:50,133 --> 00:18:52,300
Diego was the only one
with me in the car.

343
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:54,967
He could have planted that.

344
00:18:55,133 --> 00:18:56,433
I don't understand.

345
00:18:58,267 --> 00:19:00,533
He's your best friend, right?

346
00:19:00,667 --> 00:19:03,300
Why would he do that?

347
00:19:03,433 --> 00:19:04,600
I don't know either.

348
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:09,967
I noticed Diego is fond
of luxurious stuff.

349
00:19:10,100 --> 00:19:12,333
Maybe he was blinded by money.

350
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:15,067
I used to trust that
person a lot,

351
00:19:15,200 --> 00:19:17,367
but now, I don't.

352
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:20,367
Can you please tell my wife
and daughter not to trust him?

353
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:22,567
Your daughter doesn't trust me.

354
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:27,700
She won't listen to me even if I
tell her that it came from you.

355
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,667
You know, Andrew,
you're a reporter.

356
00:19:30,833 --> 00:19:33,333
You're very resourceful.

357
00:19:33,467 --> 00:19:36,267
You know what to do to make her
trust you.

358
00:19:38,500 --> 00:19:41,400
Andrew, I know we don't know
each other,

359
00:19:41,533 --> 00:19:43,433
but if you're going to help me,

360
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:47,267
can you go all out?

361
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:49,067
Please watch over my wife
and daughter.

362
00:19:50,467 --> 00:19:52,733
Help me protect my family.

363
00:19:57,067 --> 00:19:58,600
I'm begging you.

364
00:20:15,300 --> 00:20:17,467
You know, sit down for now.

365
00:20:17,600 --> 00:20:19,200
Come on.

366
00:20:19,333 --> 00:20:20,500
Thank you.

367
00:20:20,633 --> 00:20:22,767
Stop calling your Godfather.

368
00:20:22,900 --> 00:20:24,667
He might be working.

369
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,500
Come on, eat first.
Your plate is clean.

370
00:20:27,633 --> 00:20:30,267
I've been trying to contact him
for a while now.

371
00:20:30,400 --> 00:20:31,667
I've called him a few times
and texted him.

372
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,300
Not a single answer, nothing.

373
00:20:33,433 --> 00:20:36,567
I just wanted to get an update
on the flash drive.

374
00:20:36,733 --> 00:20:40,967
Maybe your Godfather will call
you if he has news for you.

375
00:20:42,867 --> 00:20:44,533
I can't wait any longer.

376
00:21:57,067 --> 00:21:58,567
Are you in Bolagos? Where?

377
00:21:58,700 --> 00:21:59,567
At the precinct.

378
00:21:59,700 --> 00:22:00,700
I talked to Delgado.

379
00:22:00,833 --> 00:22:02,100
But why?

380
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:03,433
I'll go outside.

381
00:22:03,567 --> 00:22:04,267
I'll come with you.

382
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:04,867
Me too!

383
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:05,767
Can we use your car?

384
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:07,767
Get your keys.

385
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:09,767
- Thieves!
- Wait.

386
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:13,600
I trained in the psych ward
as a nurse.

387
00:22:13,733 --> 00:22:17,533
But it didn't push through,
so I focused on my family first.

388
00:22:17,700 --> 00:22:19,567
Do you want to be busy again?

389
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:22,067
How can you earn someone's
trust?

390
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:25,900
You have to win someone's
heart first

391
00:22:26,033 --> 00:22:27,967
to make them trust you.

392
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:28,867
Andrew.

393
00:22:30,033 --> 00:22:31,433
Joey On Duty?
